# unionized_mech map: Skyline. Edit while the game runs and it reloads live.
# spawn x y z yaw | box x0 y0 z0 x1 y1 z1 (visible) | cbox ... (collision only)
#
# Sized against researched Titanfall 2 numbers, converted to metres. None of it
# is official: Respawn has never published map dimensions, so the footprints are
# community estimates and the rest is measured community work or stated design
# philosophy. What the research actually pinned down:
#
#   storey height      5 m       (a round 200 engine units, measured in Apex)
#   single doorway     1.6 m     double 3.0 m
#   wallrun face       ~20 m     from a 1.75 s wallrun at wallrun speed
#   parallel walls     6-8 m     inside what one wall jump crosses
#   mech lane          12-25 m   wide enough for two mechs to pass and dodge
#   engagement         20-40 m   typical, and what cover should be sized around
#   footprint          150-250 m per side for a standard 6v6 map
#
# 160 m square for ten players, at the tight end of that range. Three lanes
# north to south, in the three-lane skeleton the community reads in these maps:
#
#   west   x -58..-47   wallrun canyon, two staggered walls 7 m apart
#   centre x -12..12    mech avenue, open, broken by pillars and two bridges
#   east   x  30..70    city block, buildings at one, two and three storeys
#
# The rules the geometry follows, from Respawn's own statements:
#   - A wallrunnable face has to read as one: big, smooth, unbroken. Every wall
#     meant to be run is at least 20 m long with nothing stuck to it.
#   - Mech pathing is the floor on map size. The avenue and both cross streets
#     stay 20 m or wider and every bridge clears 6 m, above the 4.6 m chassis.
#   - Treat the floor like lava. Ground cover is deliberately sparse and low;
#     the height is on the walls and the roofs, and that is where the routes are.

spawn 0 0 70 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# West lane: the wallrun canyon.
#
# Inner faces 7 m apart, segments 20 m long, staggered 10 m so no single wall
# carries you the length of it. Run one, jump the gap, land the next. 8 m tall,
# which puts their tops on the mid layer rather than the roofs.
box -58 0 -70 -56 8 -50
box -58 0 -30 -56 8 -10
box -58 0 10 -56 8 30
box -58 0 50 -56 8 70
box -49 0 -60 -47 8 -40
box -49 0 -20 -47 8 0
box -49 0 20 -47 8 40
box -49 0 60 -47 8 76

# Canyon mouth, south: a low block to mantle onto so the run can be entered at
# speed from the spawn side rather than from a standing start.
box -54 0 74 -50 2 78

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# West field: the training ground, between the canyon and the avenue.

# Wall kick shaft. Faces 4 m apart, inside the 4.1 m a wall jump carries. Each
# kick tops out 1.14 m above the last, so the perch is a climb.
box -40 0 -34 -32 6 -32.5
box -40 0 -28.5 -32 6 -27
box -40 6 -34 -32 7 -27

# Mantle stairs: each step one vault higher than the last.
box -42 0 14 -38 1 18
box -37 0 14 -33 2 18
box -32 0 14 -28 3 18
box -27 0 14 -23 4 18

# Slide gate. 1.1 m of clearance: taller than the 1.0 m crouched hull, shorter
# than the 1.8 m standing one. The only way through is fast and crouched, which
# gives sliding a job on flat ground that speed alone cannot do.
box -44 1.1 44 -24 3.2 46

# Mid-layer platforms, reachable off the canyon tops, dropping into the avenue.
box -30 4 -8 -22 5 4
box -22 4 -4 -16 5 4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Centre lane: the mech avenue.
#
# 24 m of clear width down the middle so two chassis can pass and still dodge.
# The length would be a 160 m sightline if it were left alone, so it is broken
# by pillars set alternately either side of the centre line: cover you take at a
# diagonal, which keeps engagements at the 20-40 m the weapons are tuned for.
box -8 0 -58 -4 9 -54
box 4 0 -38 8 9 -34
box -8 0 -18 -4 9 -14
box 4 0 14 8 9 18
box -8 0 34 -4 9 38
box 4 0 54 8 9 58

# Central landmark: a courtyard at the crossroads, walled by four one-storey
# corner blocks. Their tops see down all three lanes, which is what makes the
# middle worth contesting, and the steps on the south-west corner are the way
# up. The middle itself stays open because the mech is parked on it.
box 9 0 -18 17 5 -10
box -17 0 -18 -9 5 -10
box 9 0 10 17 5 18
box -17 0 10 -9 5 18
box -13 0 6 -9 1.6 10
box -13 1.6 2 -9 3.2 6

# Bridges over the avenue, north and south. Decks at 6 m, which clears the
# 4.6 m chassis underneath, and they join the west mid layer to the east roofs
# so the upper route runs the full width of the map instead of dead-ending.
box -20 6 -32 20 7 -28
box -20 6 28 20 7 32
box -20 0 -32 -16 6 -28
box 16 0 -32 20 6 -28
box -20 0 28 -16 6 32
box 16 0 28 20 6 32

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# East lane: the city block.
#
# Two columns of buildings with an 8 m alley between them, wallrunnable on both
# sides down its whole length. Heights step through one, two and three storeys
# so the roofs are a route with its own climbs rather than one flat plane.
box 30 0 -76 46 10 -52
box 54 0 -76 70 5 -52
box 30 0 -44 46 5 -20
box 54 0 -44 70 10 -20
box 30 0 -12 46 15 12
box 54 0 -12 70 10 12
box 30 0 20 46 5 44
box 54 0 20 70 15 44
box 30 0 52 46 10 76
box 54 0 52 70 5 76

# Step run into the block. 0.4 m risers, under the 0.457 m step height, so this
# is walked up at full speed rather than vaulted. Kerbs should never cost you
# momentum.
box 20 0 -8 26 0.4 -4
box 20 0 -4 26 0.8 0
box 20 0 0 26 1.2 4
box 20 0 4 26 1.6 8

# Slide gate, east approach.
box 24 1.1 -46 44 3.2 -44

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross streets, east-west, at the thirds. 20 m clear so a chassis can turn
# through them, and they are what stops the three lanes being three corridors.
box -16 0 -50 -12 6 -46
box 12 0 -50 16 6 -46
box -16 0 46 -12 6 50
box 12 0 46 16 6 50

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Outer margins: sparse cover, so the edges are crossable but never safe.
box -76 0 -20 -70 3 -14
box -76 0 30 -70 3 36
box 74 0 -30 80 3 -24
box 74 0 40 80 3 46
box -20 0 -74 -14 3 -68
box 14 0 -74 20 3 -68

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Perimeter: nobody leaves the arena, and the walls are tall enough to run on.
cbox -82 0 -82 82 25 -80
cbox -82 0 80 82 25 82
cbox -82 0 -82 -80 25 82
cbox 80 0 -82 82 25 82

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bot waypoints. Auto-linked on load to neighbours within 20 m with a clear
# line at chest height. Grown outward from the spawn so every one is reachable
# from both team spawns, which sim_tests asserts: an island of waypoints is a
# bot that stands still forever. Spread to cover all three lanes, the alley
# included, rather than placed on landmarks.
node -18 0 78
node -60 0 72
node 0 0 72
node 48 0 72
node -78 0 66
node -42 0 66
node 18 0 66
node -24 0 60
node -6 0 54
node 48 0 54
node -72 0 48
node 24 0 48
node -42 0 42
node -12 0 36
node 48 0 36
node -66 0 30
node 6 0 30
node 78 0 30
node -36 0 24
node 24 0 24
node -18 0 18
node 54 0 18
node -60 0 12
node 72 0 12
node -78 0 6
node 18 0 6
node -24 0 0
node 0 0 0
node 48 0 0
node -54 0 -6
node 78 0 -6
node -72 0 -12
node -30 0 -18
node 6 0 -18
node -48 0 -24
node 24 0 -24
node 48 0 -24
node 72 0 -24
node -66 0 -30
node -24 0 -36
node 0 0 -36
node -42 0 -42
node 24 0 -42
node 48 0 -42
node 72 0 -42
node -60 0 -48
node -78 0 -54
node -30 0 -54
node -12 0 -54
node 6 0 -54
node 24 0 -60
node 48 0 -60
node 78 0 -60
node -72 0 -72
node -36 0 -72
node 0 0 -72
node -54 0 -78
node -18 0 -78
node 18 0 -78
node 36 0 -78
node 54 0 -78
node 72 0 -78
